# Right-click the sidebar's divider — the one-cell edge between the
# left column and the editor, at column 30 of a 120-wide frame (the
# window share: a fifth, never under 30). The menu: the width by the
# config or by hand, the column's two ways out of sight, and its side.
write whole_at_thirty.md "one\n"
expect screen contains "whole_at_thirty.md "
rightclick 30 10
expect screen contains "Reset width"
expect screen contains "Set width…"
expect screen contains "Hide sidebar"
expect screen contains "Auto-hide sidebar"
expect screen contains "Move sidebar to the right"
# Set width… takes a share of the window: 40% of 120 is 48 cells, so
# the divider moves to column 48.
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "Sidebar width (cells, or a share like 25%)"
type "40%"
key enter
expect screen contains "sidebar width: 48"
rightclick 48 10
expect screen contains "Reset width"
# Junk is refused and the width stays.
key down
key enter
type "wide"
key enter
expect screen contains "sidebar width: a number of cells or a share like 25%"
rightclick 48 10
expect screen contains "Reset width"
# Reset width: back to the share — the divider at 30 again.
key enter
rightclick 30 10
expect screen contains "Move sidebar to the right"
# Move sidebar to the right: the explorer goes to the right column; the
# row now offers the way back.
key end
key enter
expect screen contains "sidebar: right side"
